    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **54 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system.\n\n**`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`**\n- Added a new read-time derived `getMembershipPoints()`: starts at 0; `+2` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount` is 0, `+2` when `householdSize >= 3`, `+3` when tenure (days since `registrationDate`) exceeds 365.\n- Rewrote `getMembershipLevel()` to band those points: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+). The old cap-3 rule that computed the level directly from the factors is gone.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n- Added the `membershipPoints` schema property (int, `readOnly`, min 0) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it alongside `membershipLevel`.\n- Updated `membershipLevel`'s description and bounds (now `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 4`).\n\nBoth fields are now returned. A fresh owner with an email and no namesake scores 3 points \u2192 level 2; the only route to level 4 (6+ points) is tenure (+3), which a new owner never has \u2014 matching the new acceptance tests (Cp15, Cp23, Cp24, Cp39, Cp40).",
