    "probe_text": "The `owners.POST.yml` pipeline is live (the OfficeFloor starter is in `pom.xml`), and every step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole thing is one transaction that commits once at the end. Here is the full ordered sequence for **POST /api/owners**.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without that role the request is rejected (403) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Ordered steps\n\n1. **ValidateOwnerFields** \u2014 normalizes `address` in place, then requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` to be non-null/non-blank (checked *after* address normalization). Any missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400) naming each offender. Publishes the validated body.\n2. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 rewrites telephone to E.164 in place (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; `+` keeps its country code, otherwise assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`). Must be 8\u201315 digits; `+61` requires 9 national digits, `+1` requires 10. Otherwise \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n3. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 email is optional; if present, validate syntax and lower-case it in place. Present-but-invalid \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400).\n4. **RejectDisposableEmailDomain** \u2014 if an email is present and its domain is on the disposable blocklist (e.g. mailinator.com) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n5. **DeriveHouseholdId** \u2014 computes `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over normalized `lastName`+`postcode` and publishes it (null when no postcode). *No mutation yet.*\n6. **EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 scans all existing owners: (a) identity-key duplicate `telephone|email|householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409), always; (b) same `householdId` \u2192 409 **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold`.\n7. **EnsureCityCapacity** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); at \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n8. **EnsureDailyOwnerLimit** \u2014 computes the effective registration date (supplied or today) adjusted to a business day, counts owners already registered that day; at \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n9. **BuildOwner** \u2014 maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper` and publishes it. *(entity now exists)*\n10. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 postcode optional; if present must be 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region must fall in range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099). Otherwise \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n11. **AssignHousehold** \u2014 stamps the derived `householdId` onto the owner (skipped when null).\n12. **AssignHouseholdSize** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = 1 (this owner) + existing owners sharing the `householdId`; 1 when no household.\n13. **ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate** \u2014 if a supplied `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n14. **DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate** \u2014 resolves date (supplied or today), rolls a weekend forward to Monday, and stores it on the owner.\n15. **AssignBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > 80 owners already registered that business day (excludes this owner).\n16. **AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`, HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n17. **AssignNamesakeCount** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive; excludes this owner).\n18. **AssignMembershipNumber** \u2014 sets `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>` using the registration year's last two digits.\n19. **DetectPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`: true (with lowest matching id) when an existing owner shares `lastName`+`postcode` but has a different telephone and is not in the same household; false otherwise.\n20. **SaveOwner** \u2014 persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (id assigned).\n21. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 logs one line to the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel); read-only.\n22. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n## Worth noting on the ordering\n- **Duplicate/capacity/limit checks (steps 6\u20138) run before postcode validation (step 10)**, yet step 6\u2019s household key and step 8\u2019s day bucket already depend on postcode/date. So a request with an *invalid* postcode can still be rejected as a 409/429 duplicate/capacity error before it ever reaches the 400 postcode check.\n- The telephone/email/address normalizations (1\u20133) are **in-place mutations of the shared `@Val` body**, so all later comparisons and the stored entity use the normalized forms.\n- Status codes above come from the matching handlers under `officefloor/escalation/`; anything unmatched falls through to Spring\u2019s `@RestControllerAdvice`."
